## Learnings 

1. Frequently used framework contracts and best practices should be considered and implemented within the code.
2. Automated unit tests should be used along with interactive test cases to cater all possible inputs.
3. For a complex method, it's important to run all possible inputs in an automated unit test. If the test fails, interpret the failure and work towards a corrective action.

The given test helps verify the conditions in the contract. This test ensures that the .NET ArrayList.Contains method behaves as expected for the intended inputs while using Pex automated unit test for getting all the preconditions inputs. 

Please note that, this test may fail for edge cases. The contracts are designed for robustness in most common scenarios. The contract also assumes that the Count property of the list (ArrayList) is non-negative for all tests, since a negative Count value does not make logical sense. However, this may vary as per the actual implementation of ArrayList class in .NET Framework, and one should be careful while using it in a real system. 

This test will help you understand how we can automatically verify the behavior of the unit by checking its precondition, post-condition and also how we debug it if the test fails. This is a manual step and more of an art than a science, since it can be depended on the complexity of the methods to be tested. Automated unit test will help you to save this manual work.
